meta {
  name: List an archive's contents
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/sources/{{scopeSourceId}}/documents/archive?doc_id={{scopeDocId}}
}

docs {
  A `.zip` ingests as ONE document (its members' text concatenated — see
  `ingest/extract._extract_zip`), so `List a source's documents` otherwise shows it as one
  opaque row. This recovers the member list — and any files it skipped, and why — from the
  document's own extracted text (there's no separate column for it), for the document
  browser's expand-to-see-contents view.

  `doc_id` is one of the `doc_id` values from `List a source's documents`'s response. Returns
  `{"members": [...], "notes": [...]}` — empty lists (not an error) for a document that isn't
  an archive.
}
